# Dates and times — US Eastern

For **user-visible dates and times** in this repo (events, “today” logic, seed data meant to read as Pavilion-local), treat **US Eastern** as canonical.

## Implementation

- Use IANA **`America/New_York`** (see `EVENTS_TIME_ZONE` in [`src/lib/mit-sailing/nyTime.ts`](src/lib/mit-sailing/nyTime.ts); event seed rows also use the same constants from [`src/data/mit-sailing/eventsSeed.ts`](src/data/mit-sailing/eventsSeed.ts)) for formatting and **calendar-day** comparisons in that context.
- **Do not** use the viewer’s local time zone for those surfaces unless the product explicitly requires it.

## EST vs EDT

- Do not hard-code a single “EST” UTC offset year-round. Use **`America/New_York`** so EST and EDT apply correctly.
- **`ET`** is fine as a display suffix; avoid promising “EST” during daylight saving.

## Seed data

- Store instants as **ISO 8601**; derive display with `America/New_York` via `Intl` or shared helpers.
